    "turn_text": "because I didn't. So had I known my time was going to be this short and I said in multiple interviews over the last four years and it just hit me the other day because I had said over and over again, the people will say like, where do you get this like this? this passion and this fire from, like, what sustained you? And I would say, I felt this urgency and this weeping and never went away. And so we'll just go, go, go, get a bill for reparations, get a bill to deal with police and get a bill to do, you know, all of these, get a bill to help the unhouse, get a bill, like fight, fight, fight, get the ERA, you know, help the people with Gaza, like fight, fight, fight. Um, but had I known that I only had those for years, I would have flipped more tables instead of having that one protest on the house steps, probably, you know, for the eviction moratorium.",
