    "turn_text": "I respect that so much. I think that a lot of people's hindsight says, what could I have done to preserve my position, my seat, my title? Your hindsight is saying, what could I have done to tear it up even more, right? If I was only going to be there for a limited time only, how was I going to wreck shop in ways that moved us forward even more than I have? And I think that this is an open question that people have, especially right now for the Democratic Party, right? That like, if everybody spent the last election calling the person who was about to be inaugurated a fascist and actually believed it, then how do you behave when the fascist takes office and you are standing opposite him on the Capitol steps? Do you think that given how this election cycle went, the Democrats as they do their soul searching, do they have an image problem? Do they have a messaging problem? Or is it a reality problem? Does there just need to be a whole shaking at the table?",
